/E (In PHP, superglobals are special built-in variables that are always accessible from any part of a script, regardless of scope. They are predefined by PHP to allow developers to easily access data sent by the client \(such as form input\), information about the server, session data, cookies, or uploaded files. Superglobals are critical because they form the primary interface between the client \(browser\) and the server-side PHP script.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
